OL,3,GNEWSATeen's brain haemorrhage began
OL,4,Awith headache at a party
OL,5,
OL,6,FLidia Connolly was at a party when she
OL,7,Fcomplained of a slight headache.
OL,9,FWhen she didn't return from the
OL,10,Fbathroom, she was found unresponsive
OL,11,Fand, according to her mum Penny,
OL,12,Fcompletely still and "just nothing".
OL,14,FIt was a brain haemorrhage that caused
OL,15,Fher to fall ill and the bleed would
OL,16,Fprove to be fatal. She was 19.
OL,23,APub: 28-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
